# CMake
cmake-build-debug/
cmake-build-release/
build/
bin/
lib/
# BUILD TREES AND INSTALL PREFIXES BY POLICY, NOT BY ENUMERATION.
#
# These used to be listed one directory at a time, and the comment here said
# so outright: build-host/ and install-host/ each with "own name, own ignore
# line" as the stated shape. THAT ENUMERATION FELL BEHIND THREE TIMES --
# build-pb/, build-ci-consumer/ and install-ci/ were each untracked and NOT
# ignored. The last two are the expensive ones: they made every provenance
# line on 2026-09-10 report dirty=true, across every realm, in a phase whose
# recurring subject was whether a tally's provenance could be trusted at all.
#
# The root .gitignore reached this conclusion for ROOT trees and states the
# reason above its own /build-*/ rule: "An enumeration was guaranteed to fall
# behind the moment the parameter existed, and did, within the hour." That
# comment has been sitting one directory away from an enumeration doing
# exactly that.
#
# A pattern needs no guard, which is the point: an enumeration can only be
# kept current by someone remembering, so it needs a test to catch them
# forgetting. This cannot fall behind.
#
# SAFE because nothing here that is not a build artifact begins with
# build- or install-: the real directories are assets/ cmake/ docs/ engine/
# examples/ include/ scripts/ src/ tests/ vendor/. A future source directory
# wanting one of those prefixes has to say so here, which is the right place
# for that argument to happen.
#
# What these cover, since the names no longer explain themselves:
#   build-ninja/<preset>/        scripts/build.ps1's dev-loop trees
#   build-<anything>/            hand-configured trees (-DSPADE_VULKAN=OFF,
#                                a consumer-smoke build, ...)
#   install-<anything>/          cmake --install prefixes, e.g. the one an
#                                out-of-tree consumer resolves find_package
#                                (spade) against
build-*/
install-*/
# gtest_discover_tests() runs discovery with the tests' WORKING_DIRECTORY,
# which is the source root (tests/CMakeLists.txt), and CMake 4.x leaves its
# --gtest_output file there: a build artifact, never source.
/cmake_test_discovery_*.json
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
# CMake's own in-source outputs, by name. Never a blanket *.cmake: that hid
# three authored helpers (tests/AppendSpadeLabels.cmake, cmake/SpadeSlang.cmake,
# tools/flow_movie/stamp_identity.cmake), and the last never reached git, so
# every fresh checkout failed to configure (74736cb, 2026-10-13). CMake's
# generated Find*.cmake and package-config files live in the build and install
# trees, which build/, build-*/ and install-*/ above already ignore.
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
CPackConfig.cmake
CPackSourceConfig.cmake
Makefile

